{"kind":"assert","text":"LL-1 note at 1f8173ef: it follows ruling 8568a680. Two points to add in the same notes-only head, before or after the checker's verdict on e01dda1a:\n1. A late open after eviction. A member enters (open, key k1) and later leaves, and eviction removes the item and its retry records. If a delayed retry of the k1 open then arrives inside the intent's lifetime, it is judged fresh and can open the item again: a ghost presence row until its lease timer expires. State this case, the bound on it (the O2 retry cutoff d58ff62f and the lease timer), and whether the open's guard refuses it. If no bound short of one lease applies, say so plainly. The cost is one stale row for at most one lease. I accept that, but the note must not leave it unstated.\n2. Final counts and final reads. After eviction, the live summary reports 0 for every final state, and LiveReads.items returns an empty page. That is a visible change. Name the live definitions and clients that read final counts or final items today (Pinboard, the map application and the shipped examples). Either confirm none does, or name each one and what it shows instead.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}